  "surprise": "P34 x P32 head split, 5 ALiBi heads (standard 5-head slopes 1/3.03, 1/9.19, 1/27.9, 1/84.4, 1/256) + 3 NoPE instead of 115's 4+4 (only N_ALIBI changed, 4,800,000 params), scored 634/595/621 on seeds 0/1/2 vs 115-fable's 639/646/609. Exact means 616.67 vs 631.33, -14.67, paired -5/-51/+12, inside the registered -40..+35 range (central 0). Discard. The registered mechanism is REFUTED in direction: the extra, steeper recency head made the RL start worse, not cleaner. Round-1 targets solved 532/679/591 (mean 601) vs 718/756/691 (722). Round-1 sample acc 0.164/0.290/0.238 vs 0.318/0.301/0.315. Round-1 parse failures 22577/10970/16732 of 48,000 = 47/23/35% vs 25/22/18% (predicted 15-25%; 113 all-ALiBi: 50/30/64%). Cap-6 fit was unchanged: 4294/4197/4254 steps (115: 4204/4218/4263), final val loss 0.0825/0.0808/0.0776 vs 0.0826/0.0806/0.0792, held-out greedy 0.985/0.984/0.982 vs 0.9815/0.983/0.9845. So this is the same length-extrapolation failure as 113 and 117-fable, in milder form. RL repaired most of it: parse failures 7182/5064/4795 at r2 and 4662/3551/3694 at r4 (115 r4: 4472/3753/4408), r1->r4 +569/+386/+509 (mean +488 vs 115's +384), r4 RL-solved 1101/1065/1100 (mean 1089 vs 1106). The eval frontier did not recover: ge10 91/90/92 vs 103/97/89, ge11 22/18/19 vs 25/23/19, ge12 4/3/5 vs 5/4/4, L* 11/11/12, eval parse failures 10821/9849/13291 of 70,912 vs 11563/11640/13004. Surprise: pretraining loss and downstream RL pull the slope table in opposite directions. 116-claude's learned slopes steepened the local head toward 1/2.4-1/3 (what this table supplies) and also started RL lower; this fixed version of that request costs ~120 round-1 targets. The 3-point quadratic over NoPE-head count (peak near 3) was wrong; with this point the curve reads 0 NoPE 606 (113), 3 NoPE 617 (119), 4 NoPE 631 (115), 8 NoPE 547 (111, RoPE-removed base). Confound: two things changed together (one fewer NoPE head, and a steeper steepest slope 1/3.03 vs 1/4 with a denser mid-range), so this run does not say which one hurt. The natural next test goes the other way: 4+4 with gentler slopes (e.g. 1/8..1/512) or 3 ALiBi + 5 NoPE. Seed 2 ran on a slow pod (173-192 samples/s in rounds 2-4, Lean gate 181 s wall at r2), total 1925 s vs 1506/1612 s on seeds 0/1.",
